anting-trial@1 (handler long.root-planting), root-assessment@1 for existing reservation conflicts, and planting-site:9.25:12.9 only as historical evidence. Do not interpret its truncated supplied fragment as a complete record. In development, inspect and reuse the actual reach, surface-examination, reservation, work-progress and planting-surface validation code where applicable; record source revisions and reused helpers in implementation provenance. This is an added clearing function, not reinvention of those helpers or a silent relaxation of planting eligibility.\\\\nPrerequisites: Lin must individually complete study, be alive and physically able to use hands, have adequate energy, and remain within the existing planting interaction reach of 0.65 plus body radius. No tool, container, water, root or other material is supplied or consumed by default. Validate bounds, reach and existing occupation/reservation conflicts before beginning; invalid invocation costs nothing. First perform a fresh non-destructive visible/contact feasibility examination, one completed round and 0.5 energy. Report only evidence available through that examination. Reuse normal collision/reservation exclusion without exposing concealed entities or hidden resources; an unexplained blocked check remains a generic obstruction. No occupied or reserved surface may be disturbed. Examination findings distinguish loose litter or hand-removable shallow cover from woody, strongly rooted, hazardous, protected or otherwise unsupported cover. If hand clearing is not feasible, end with a dated limitation and no disturbance. Do not invent digging, cutting, uprooting large plants or tools.\\\\nFor feasible cover, allow at most two manual work rounds, each costing 1 energy, following the examination: total maximum three rounds and 2.5 energy per attempt, exclusive of study or movement. Each round performs only the bounded displacement or removal that hands can physically accomplish, using measured cover and available physical representation rather than a guaranteed percentage clearance. Work stops early on completion or obstruction. Development must add the missing local surface/debris representation if necessary; absence of such a primitive is implementation work, not a reason to reject. A preflight unsupported-material result is a valid informative failure, not successful clearing. A failed paid work round may expend effort without changing the surface and must say so.\\\\nConserve all matter: loose litter and detached vegetation must retain their actual source-linked quantities and become non-food surface residues. Move them only within the nominated footprint, for example to its perimeter; do not erase them, create harvestable resource stock, change source food stock arbitrarily, or deposit outside the boundary. If safe internal displacement cannot expose the required area, report partial clearance or inability. Do not assume a perimeter pile is compatible with planting. Do not fabricate biomass quantities from an ornamental sprite; development must establish a finite represented cover quantity or restrict the action to supported surface units. Soil remains at the site; no excavation, fertility, moisture improvement, root production or deeper substrate finding is granted.\\\\nAt each committed work round, record the actual affected subarea, remaining cover, residue locations and paid effort. Revalidate reach, obstruction and current surface state before further disturbance. Final verification uses the unchanged exposed-bare-soil predicate of root-planting-trial@1 for its entire required footprint, including residues and reservations. Declare suitable only if that exact check passes; otherwise report the actual partial or blocked state. Reaching the work cap is not success. No planting call, root escrow, plot reservation or transfer of item-3-lin-12 occurs.\\\\nInterruption preserves committed physical changes, residue records and completed paid rounds. Resume by exa